| Strategy               | Description                                                                                   | Code Example                                                                                       |
|------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Exponential Backoff    | Reduces the frequency of retries over time.                                                        | ```typescriptfunction exponentialBackoff(retries: number, maxDelay: number): number { return Math.min(maxDelay, Math.pow(2, retries) * 1000); }``` |
| Jitter                 | Adds randomness to the backoff period to avoid synchronized retries.                               | ```typescriptfunction jitteredBackoff(retries: number, baseDelay: number): number { const jitter = Math.random() * baseDelay; return baseDelay + jitter; }``` |
| Circuit Breaker        | Prevents repeated attempts to call a failing service by opening the circuit after a certain number of failures. | ```typescriptclass CircuitBreaker { private open: boolean = false; private failures: number = 0; private maxFailures: number = 5; private resetTimeout: number = 30000; public execute(): boolean { if (this.open) { return false; } try { // Call the service return true; } catch (error) { this.failures++; if (this.failures >= this.maxFailures) { this.open = true; setTimeout(() => this.open = false, this.resetTimeout); } return false; } } }``` |
| Fallback Chain         | Provides alternative paths when the primary method fails.                                        | ```typescriptclass FallbackChain { private primary: () => any; private secondary: () => any; constructor(primary: () => any, secondary: () => any) { this.primary = primary; this.secondary = secondary; } execute(): any { try { return this.primary(); } catch (error) { return this.secondary(); } } }``` |
| Graceful Degradation   | Provides reduced functionality rather than failing entirely.                                       | ```typescriptclass GracefulDegradation { private primary: () => any; private degraded: () => any; constructor(primary: () => any, degraded: () => any) { this.primary = primary; this.degraded = degraded; } execute(): any { try { return this.primary(); } catch (error) { return this.degraded(); } } }``` |
